.TH MYSTRNCPY 3 "2026-09-25" "libmyutils 1.0" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mystrncpy \- copy a bounded number of characters from a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fB#include "mystrfunctions.h"\fP
.sp
.BI "int mystrncpy(char *" dest ", const char *" src ", int " n );
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR mystrncpy ()
function copies at most
.I n
characters from the string pointed to by
.I src
into the buffer pointed to by
.IR dest .
If
.I src
is shorter than
.IR n ,
the remainder of
.I dest
up to
.I n
bytes is padded with null bytes. If
.I src
is
.I n
characters or longer, the result in
.I dest
is
.B not
null-terminated, matching the behavior of the standard
.BR strncpy (3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of characters actually copied from
.IR src .
Returns \-1 if
.I dest
or
.I src
is NULL, or if
.I n
is negative.
